API KEYS / SECRETS NEEDED BEFORE REAL LAUNCH
==============================================
Fill these in backend/.env (copy from backend/.env.example if you haven't
already). Nothing in the app crashes if these are left blank - each
feature just stays disabled/degraded until its key is added (see the
"what happens if left blank" note on each one). Delete this file once
everything below is filled in for real.


1) RAZORPAY (online payment - UPI/Cards/Netbanking)
-----------------------------------------------------
  RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
  RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
  RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

  Where to get it: Razorpay Dashboard -> Settings -> API Keys (Key ID +
  Secret). The Webhook Secret is set separately under Settings -> Webhooks
  when you add a webhook URL pointing at:
    https://<your-domain>/api/v1/storefront/payments/razorpay/webhook
  (check the exact route in backend/src/modules/storefront/storefront.routes.js
  if you rename anything).

  Also needed on the CLIENT app (client/.env - create this file, it doesn't
  exist yet):
    VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
  (same value as RAZORPAY_KEY_ID above - this one is public/safe to expose,
  it's the publishable key Razorpay Checkout.js uses in the browser).

  Current status: Online payment is COMMENTED OUT in
  client/src/pages/CheckoutPage.jsx (only Cash on Delivery is selectable
  right now) specifically because these keys were empty. Once you've added
  real keys:
    1. Uncomment the "Pay Online" radio option and its handling block in
       client/src/pages/CheckoutPage.jsx (both are clearly marked with a
       comment explaining what to uncomment together).
    2. Test a real payment end-to-end in Razorpay TEST mode first (test
       keys look the same shape as live keys, Razorpay dashboard has a
       test/live toggle) before switching to live keys.
    3. Refunds: orderRefund.service.js already calls the real Razorpay
       refund API automatically once these keys are set - no extra code
       change needed there.


1b) GOOGLE SIGN-IN (Continue with Google, on the customer /login page)
-----------------------------------------------------
  GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

  Where to get it: https://console.cloud.google.com -> APIs & Services ->
  Credentials -> Create Credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Application type
  "Web application". Under "Authorized JavaScript origins" add your real
  site origin(s) (e.g. https://www.yourstore.com, and
  http://localhost:5180 for local dev). You do NOT need a client secret -
  this uses Google's ID-token flow (the browser gets a signed token
  straight from Google; the backend just verifies it), not a server-side
  OAuth redirect.

  Also needed on the CLIENT app (client/.env - same file as
  VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID above):
    VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
  (same value as GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID - this one is public/safe to expose, it's
  what Google Identity Services uses in the browser to render the button).

  Current status: the "Continue with Google" button on /login (both the
  Create Account and Log In tabs) simply doesn't render at all until
  VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID is set - no broken button, no error shown to
  customers. The backend route (POST /auth/google) returns a clear 503
  ("Google sign-in is not configured") if hit directly without
  GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID set. Once both are added, it works immediately - no
  code changes needed, this was built already-wired, not stubbed.


2) RESEND (transactional email - order confirmation, shipping updates,
   password reset)
-----------------------------------------------------
  RESEND_API_KEY=

  Where to get it: https://resend.com -> API Keys. You'll also need to
  verify a sending domain there (or use their test domain while testing).

  Current status: notification.sender.js silently no-ops without this -
  no crash, but customers get ZERO emails right now, including password
  reset links (auth.service.js#requestPasswordReset). This is a real
  launch blocker if you want password reset or order emails to work.

  The "from" address is currently hardcoded in
  backend/src/modules/shared/notification.sender.js as
  notifications@amardeepswarnakalakendra.com - update that to match
  whatever domain you verify in Resend.


3) WHATSAPP BUSINESS API (order updates via WhatsApp)
-----------------------------------------------------
  WHATSAPP_TOKEN=
  WHATSAPP_PHONE_ID=

  Where to get it: Meta for Developers -> WhatsApp -> API Setup (needs a
  Meta Business account + a verified WhatsApp Business phone number).

  Current status: optional feature, silently disabled without these -
  order notifications still work via email once RESEND_API_KEY is set,
  this is just an additional channel.


4) CLOUDINARY (product images/videos, review photos, everything uploaded
   through Admin -> Media)
-----------------------------------------------------
  CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
  CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
  CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=

  Where to get it: https://cloudinary.com -> Dashboard (free tier is
  usually enough to start).

  Current status: without these, ANY image/video upload anywhere in the
  admin panel will fail. This is required before you can even add real
  product photos - treat this as priority #1 to fill in.


5) MONGODB (database)
-----------------------------------------------------
  MONGO_URI=

  Where to get it: MongoDB Atlas (https://mongodb.com/atlas) -> create a
  free/paid cluster -> Connect -> "Connect your application" -> copy the
  connection string, replace <user>/<password>/<cluster> with your real
  values. Do NOT point production at a localhost MongoDB.


6) REDIS (caching - geo-IP lookups, reverse-geocode cache)
-----------------------------------------------------
  REDIS_URL=

  A managed Redis (Upstash, Redis Cloud free tier, etc.) works fine for
  this app's usage. If left as the localhost default in production, geo
  lookups will just fail to connect and fall back gracefully (never
  crashes the app), but you lose the caching benefit.


7) JWT SECRETS (session security) - REQUIRED, app won't start without them
-----------------------------------------------------
  JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=
  JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=

  These currently sit in .env.example as literal placeholder text
  ("change_this_access_secret" / "change_this_refresh_secret"). The app
  DOES start with weak values like that (it only checks they're non-empty,
  not that they're strong) - but every login/session in production would
  be signed with a guessable secret. Generate two real random strings
  before going live, e.g.:
    node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"
  Run that twice, use one output for each secret. Keep them different from
  each other.


8) CORS_ORIGIN / SITE_URL (must point at your real domains)
-----------------------------------------------------
  CORS_ORIGIN=
  SITE_URL=

  CORS_ORIGIN: comma-separated list of every real frontend origin allowed
  to call this API (e.g. https://www.yourstore.com,https://admin.yourstore.com).
  Currently defaults to localhost:5173 - MUST be changed or the live
  storefront/admin will get CORS errors calling the API.

  SITE_URL: your real storefront domain (e.g. https://www.yourstore.com) -
  used to build the password-reset email link and canonical URLs. Also
  currently defaults to localhost.


9) ONE-TIME: create the first Super Admin account
-----------------------------------------------------
  Not a .env value - run this once against your production database
  (see backend/scripts/seedSuperAdmin.js for what it does):

    SUPER_ADMIN_NAME="Your Name" \
    SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL="admin@yourdomain.com" \
    SUPER_ADMIN_PHONE="9999999999" \
    SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD="a-real-strong-password" \
    npm run seed:admin

  (from inside backend/). Safe to run more than once - it does nothing if
  a Super Admin already exists.


10) OPTIONAL, NOT YET ADDED (mentioned here so you don't forget):
-----------------------------------------------------
  - Error monitoring (e.g. Sentry) - not wired into the codebase at all
    yet. If you want this, you'll need a Sentry DSN and a small amount of
    integration code added to backend/src/server.js and both frontends.
  - SMS/OTP provider (e.g. MSG91/Twilio) - not wired in. WhatsApp (#3
    above) is currently the only "text message" channel.


ALSO DONE FOR YOU IN THIS PASS (later, admin Broadcast feature):
-----------------------------------------------------
  - New "Broadcast" page in the admin panel (sidebar -> Customer
    Intelligence -> Broadcast) lets you send one message to every customer
    at once via Email + WhatsApp + an on-site announcement banner,
    together, in one click.
  - Email/WhatsApp delivery uses the exact same RESEND_API_KEY /
    WHATSAPP_TOKEN+WHATSAPP_PHONE_ID as everything else (#2 and #3 above) -
    until those are set, a broadcast will show "sent" with every
    email/WhatsApp attempt marked failed (visible in the live stats on the
    Broadcast page). The website banner channel needs no key - it works
    today.
  - Respects each customer's communication preferences (Account -> opted
    out of email/WhatsApp customers are automatically skipped, counted
    separately as "skipped" in the stats, never as "failed").
  - No job queue exists in this backend - a broadcast processes in the
    background on the same server process (chunked, ~25 customers at a
    time). Safe at this project's current customer-list scale; if the
    customer base grows into the tens of thousands, revisit with a real
    queue (e.g. BullMQ) rather than relying on this in-process loop.


ALSO DONE FOR YOU IN THIS PASS (no key needed, just flagging):
-----------------------------------------------------
  - Legal pages seeded for real: run `npm run seed:legal` (from backend/)
    to create Privacy Policy / Terms & Conditions / Shipping Policy /
    Return & Exchange Policy as real, editable CMS pages (Admin -> CMS ->
    Pages). The wording is a genuine starting template, NOT reviewed by a
    lawyer - read through each one and fill in the "[DATE - fill in]" /
    "[CITY - fill in]" placeholders, and have a lawyer review before
    relying on it.
  - Password reset (forgot/reset password) is fully built - it just needs
    RESEND_API_KEY (#2 above) to actually deliver the email.
  - Cash on Delivery order-value limit exists (COD_MAX_ORDER_VALUE env
    var, backend/src/config/env.js) but is left UNSET on purpose - it
    would strand high-value orders with no payment method while Razorpay
    is disabled. Set it once Razorpay (#1) is back online.
